<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomon Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Solomons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands is an archipelagic country in Melanesia, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, made up of six major islands and many smaller ones; its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honiara">Honiara</a> lies on Guadalcanal. People have lived there since at least 30,000 to 28,800 BCE. The Spanish navigator Álvaro de Mendaña was the first European to visit, in 1568. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the southern islands in June 1893, and the Solomon Islands campaign of 1942 to 1945 brought heavy fighting, including the Battle of Guadalcanal. Self-government came in 1976 and independence in 1978. Ethnic violence between 1998 and 2003 was ended with the arrival of the Australian-led RAMSI mission in July 2003.</p></div>
